# Routing and i18n

- Locales: `ka` (default, no prefix), `en` (`/en/…`), `ru` (`/ru/…`), `tr` (`/tr/…`). Internal hrefs are English (`/snakes/[slug]`). Public KA slugs are Georgian (`/gvelebi/giurza`). Latin locales use English pathnames (`/ru/snakes/macrovipera-lebetina`).
- Use `Link` / `getPathname` from `@/i18n/navigation`. Do not hardcode `/ka`, `/en`, `/ru`, or `/tr`.
- Edge: `src/proxy.ts`, not `middleware.ts`. Legacy `/species/{id}` 301s live there; static 301s in `next.config.ts`.
- New guide: `pathnames.ts` → `RESERVED_HUB_SLUGS` → `CLUSTER_GUIDES` + `createClusterGuideRoute` page → messages in `ka`/`en`/`ru`/`tr` → cross-locale 301s.
- Hubs: `createGroupHubRoute`. Species: `createSpeciesHubRoute`. Catch-all `[...rest]` is 404 `noindex`.
- Quiz: `QUIZ_INDEX` in `quizzes.ts`. One live quiz (`romeli-gvelia` / `which-snake` / `kakaya-zmeya` / `hangi-yilan`). No indexable result/session URLs. Do not take over `გველის ამოცნობა` (that is the identify guide).
- Title template adds ` — Reptiles`; species and quiz landings often use `title: { absolute }`.
- `www.reptiles.ge` → apex. API: `X-Robots-Tag: noindex`.
